; Point HL' at the attribute cell of a screen address
;
; Converts the screen bitmap address in HL into the attribute address of the
; same character cell and leaves it in the alternate register HL'. The low byte
; is the same in both, so only the high byte changes: bits 3-4 of H select the
; screen third (0-2), which becomes the offset from the attribute high byte.
; The drawing routines #R$6BFA and #R$6B4F then write an attribute through HL'
; (and increment it) for every cell they draw. The main register set is
; selected again on return.
; Hardware: computes an address in the attribute area ($5800-$5AFF); writes
; nothing.
;
; HL Screen bitmap address (in the first pixel row of a cell)
; O:HL' Attribute address matching HL
; O:A Corrupted
@label=SetAttrPointer
c$6C0F PUSH HL       ;
 $6C10 EXX           ;
 $6C11 POP HL        ;
 $6C12 LD A,H        ;
@isub=AND THIRD_BITS
 $6C13 AND $18       ;
 $6C15 SRA A         ;
 $6C17 SRA A         ;
 $6C19 SRA A         ;
@isub=ADD A,ATTRS_HIGH
 $6C1B ADD A,$58     ;
 $6C1D LD H,A        ;
 $6C1E EXX           ;
 $6C1F RET           ;
